--
libstdc++ 13 <sstream>: `o << 4' leaves o.str() empty.  basic_ostream<char>
::_M_insert<long> (ostream:462) is instantiated despite its `extern
template' declaration in bits/ostream.tcc (CBMC links no library, so the
definition is needed), but its body is dropped: `this->_M_num_put' is an
"unresolved member expression" because basic_ostream<char> was
instantiated from within its base basic_ios<char> (basic_ios.h names
ostreambuf_iterator, whose typedef names basic_ostream; [temp.inst]/2
requires neither) and kept basic_ios's partial member list.  Reduced to
cpp11_class_instantiated_while_its_base_is_instantiated.  An earlier
experiment deferring member typedefs (skip-elaborate) avoided the drop but
broke cpp11_set_iterate and made verification run for over 54 minutes; a
fix must keep cpp11_set_iterate.  Related:
cpp98_explicit_instantiation_of_member_function_template (ostream.tcc's
explicit instantiation definitions) and
cpp11_virtual_base_default_member_initializer (fixed).  g++ 13 accepts
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
